---

## Complexity Analysis

| Algorithm | Time Complexity | Space Complexity |
|------------|----------------|------------------|
| Minimax | O(b^d) | O(d) |
| Alpha-Beta Search | O(b^d) | O(d) |
| Heuristic Alpha-Beta Search | O(b^k) | O(k) |
| Monte-Carlo Tree Search | O(N × Simulation Length) | O(N) |

Where:

- b = Branching Factor
- d = Search Depth
- k = Depth Limit
- N = Number of Simulations

---

## Conclusion

The implementation successfully demonstrates the working of Minimax Search, Alpha-Beta Search, Heuristic Alpha-Beta Search, and Monte-Carlo Tree Search on the Tic-Tac-Toe game.

The test results confirm that the algorithms correctly identify optimal moves, while Monte-Carlo Tree Search uses simulation-based decision making to estimate move quality.
